Source DB se Export:
db2 "export to CSS_ROLE_LOCALES.ixf of ixf select * from DEV_BIP_T.CSS_ROLE_LOCALES"

Target DB me Table Create Karo:
Agar target schema BIP_USER hai, to pehle table create karo:

db2 "CREATE TABLE BIP_USER.CSS_ROLE_LOCALES LIKE DEV_BIP_T.CSS_ROLE_LOCALES;

Import into Different Schema:
db2 "IMPORT FROM CSS_ROLE_LOCALES.ixf OF IXF INSERT INTO BIP_USER.CSS_ROLE_LOCALES"

Ya agar table khali hai aur data replace karna hai:
db2 "IMPORT FROM CSS_ROLE_LOCALES.ixf OF IXF REPLACE INTO BIP_USER.CSS_ROLE_LOCALES"

Faster Option (LOAD)

Large data ke liye:
db2 "LOAD FROM CSS_ROLE_LOCALES.ixf OF IXF INSERT INTO BIP_USER.CSS_ROLE_LOCALES"

Load ke baad zarurat pade to:
SET INTEGRITY FOR BIP_USER.CSS_ROLE_LOCALES IMMEDIATE CHECKED;

===========================================================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
Export with LOB Data:

db2 "EXPORT TO CSS_ROLE_LOCALES.ixf OF IXF SELECT * FROM DEV_BIP_T.CSS_ROLE_LOCALES"

Ya explicitly LOB files generate karne ke liye:
db2 "EXPORT TO CSS_ROLE_LOCALES.ixf OF IXF LOBS TO ./lobdir SELECT * FROM DEV_BIP_T.CSS_ROLE_LOCALES"

Import into Different Schema

Pehle target schema me table create karo:
CREATE TABLE NEW_SCHEMA.CSS_ROLE_LOCALES LIKE DEV_BIP_T.CSS_ROLE_LOCALES;

Phir import:
db2 "IMPORT FROM CSS_ROLE_LOCALES.ixf OF IXF
LOBS FROM ./lobdir
INSERT INTO NEW_SCHEMA.CSS_ROLE_LOCALES"

Ya large data ho to:
db2 "LOAD FROM CSS_ROLE_LOCALES.ixf OF IXF LOBS FROM ./lobdir INSERT INTO NEW_SCHEMA.CSS_ROLE_LOCALES"

Table me LOB columns check karne ke liye:

SELECT COLNAME, TYPENAME
FROM SYSCAT.COLUMNS
WHERE TABSCHEMA='DEV_BIP_T'
  AND TABNAME='CSS_ROLE_LOCALES'
  AND TYPENAME IN ('BLOB','CLOB','DBCLOB');

